    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/associate-vice-president-of-the-oklahoma-cooperative-extension-service-bf9949-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Cooperative Extension Service BF9949",
      "description": "Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Cooperative Extension Service BF9949 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States OKState.edu Applicant Login My Settings University Human Resources MENU Open Main Menu CLOSE Close Main Menu Home All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Home All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Applicant Login My Settings Kiosk mode Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Cooperative Extension Service BF9949 Apply Now Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Cooperative Extension Service BF9949 494914 Stillwater DIV AGRICULTRL SCI & NATURAL RESRCS (STW) Faculty PhD Add to favorites View favorites Campus OSU-Stillwater Contact Name & Email Jane Carpenter, jane.carpenter@okstate.edu Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm with occasional evenings and weekends. Appointment Length Regular Continuous/Until Further Notice Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, please include a resume, cover letter and contact information for three professional references. Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by 2026-11-01 to ensure full consideration. About this Position The Division of Agricultural Sciences and Natural Resources (DASNR), Oklahoma State University, invites nominations and applications for the position of Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Cooperative Extension Service (OCES). This 12-month position is administratively responsible to the Vice President, Dean and Director, Division of Agricultural Sciences and Natural Resources. The OCES employs more than 400 faculty, professional, and support staff. Employees are located on the OSU campus and in more than 80 locations throughout Oklahoma. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to the land-grant mission. The OCES Associate Vice President is the chief operating officer of OCES and will provide transformative statewide, regional, and national leadership in fostering high-quality and effective Cooperative Extension Service programs relevant to Oklahoma needs. The incumbent will: •    Lead long-range program planning, implementation and reporting for the OCES system. •    Work with the DASNR Vice President, Dean and Director to administer programs, personnel, and fiscal affairs. •    Provide leadership to increase revenue for OCES with county, state, federal, and private sources. •    Provide leadership for engagement with county and state leaders and legislators to enhance extension programming. •    Actively seek input on program needs and to garner support for OCES from food and agricultural organizations, natural resource organizations, community health and wellness organizations, and other stakeholders. •    Help lead campus-wide initiatives on Extension and coordinate with the Associate Vice President, Oklahoma Agricultural Experiment Station (OSU Ag Research), Associate Dean of the Ferguson College of Agriculture (Academic Programs), the Deans and extension leads from other Colleges at Oklahoma State University including the Colleges or Education and Human Sciences, Engineering, Architecture and Technology, Spears School of Business, Veterinary Medicine, and Arts & Sciences to achieve effective coordination of Extension programs. •    Manage day-to-day operations of OCES administrative issues. •    Maintain an active role in regional and national organizations such as the Association of Southern Region Extension Directors and Association of Public and Land Grant Universities. •    Actively engage with the USDA National Institute for Food and Agriculture, the Oklahoma Department of Agriculture, Food and Forestry, and other federal and state agencies to coordinate Extension and outreach efforts across organizations to position OCES for funding opportunities. •    Provide leadership for full compliance with the Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Program in the OCES. •    Serve as a member of DASNR’s executive team and coordinate with the Dean and VP, Associate Dean of the Ferguson College of Agriculture, and the Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Agricultural Experiment Station to advance OSU Agriculture and ensure synergies with teaching, research, and Extension missions. Required Qualifications A terminal degree in a discipline related to the Cooperative Extension Service mission is preferred; exceptions may be made for individuals with exceptional leadership and administrative experience related to the OCES mission; (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date) Experience leading a complex organization with multiple layers of direct reports is strongly preferred; A comprehensive understanding of non-formal youth and adult education and program development processes; A demonstrated ability to serve effectively as an administrative leader; a proven ability to communicate effectively; and a demonstrated capability to manage personnel and budgets; An understanding of issues important to Oklahoma agriculture, families, youth and communities and a grasp of the means to provide visionary and progressive leadership in the development of innovative programs; A thorough understanding of all levels, programming areas, and aspects of the Cooperative Extension Service is essential with the ability to strengthen relationships with constituency groups at the county, state, and federal level. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience in the Cooperative Extension System is preferred. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 5c023d15 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Cooperative Extension Executive/Administrative/Managerial Cooperative Extension Executive/Administrative/Managerial Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) b7d122c8 Last Name (required) 031084f2 Email (required) 28148a5d Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) 26fc8e9e Last Name (required) e83c5bff Email (required) 9538bbc5 Save this job for later 4709f047 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Extension Learning and Development Program Director CS9612 Stillwater DIV AGRICULTRL SCI & NATURAL RESRCS (STW) Assistant Director Upward Bound-FS9967 Oklahoma City OKLAHOMA CITY (OKC) Teacher Assistant AS7577 Stillwater EDUCATION & HUMAN SCIENCES (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) 413071fa Last Name (required) 29d4887b Email (required) 7570cb23 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you University Human Resources Part of the System Operations Oklahoma State University 201 General Academic Building Oklahoma State University Stillwater, OK 74078 (map) (405) 744-5449 | Contact Us Follow US News Events Social Media Directory Facebook LinkedIn Oklahoma State University Campus & Parking Maps All OSU Institutions Careers @ OSU Hire OSU Grads © 2026 Oklahoma State University. All rights reserved. Accessibility Services Campus Safety Access & Community Impact EEO Statement Ethics Point Privacy Notice Terms of Service Trademarks Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our tra