    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/post-doctoral-fellowship-gf1740-tulsa-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "UniversityHuman Resources",
      "description": "Post Doctoral Fellowship GF1740 - Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States OKState.edu Applicant Login My Settings University Human Resources MENU Open Main Menu CLOSE Close Main Menu Home All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Home All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Applicant Login My Settings Kiosk mode Post Doctoral Fellowship GF1740 Apply Now Post Doctoral Fellowship GF1740 494975 Tulsa CENTER FOR HEALTH SCIENCES (CHS) Faculty PhD Add to favorites View favorites Campus OSU-Center for Health Sciences Contact Name & Email Jamie Childers, Jamie.Childers@okstate.edu Work Schedule Typically, Monday - Friday 8 hour shifts Appointment Length Regular Continuous/Until Further Notice Hiring Range $ Salary Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by to ensure full consideration. About this Position This is a Grant Funded Position A Postdoctoral Fellow position is available in the laboratory of Dr. Swarup Mitra at Oklahoma State University Center for Health Sciences. This NIH-funded position is ideal for an ambitious and collaborative scientist interested in working at the intersection of neuroscience, gut microbiome biology, and neuroimmune signaling. Research Focus: Our laboratory investigates how interactions between the gut microbiome and the brain influence behavior, neural plasticity, stress susceptibility, and disease vulnerability. Current NIH-funded projects examine mechanisms by which microbial and host-derived signals influence neural circuits and cellular processes, including astrocyte and oligodendrocyte biology, neuroimmune signaling, epigenetic regulation, and behavioral adaptations. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to work across multiple experimental platforms and develop an independent research direction within the broader goals of the NIH-funded program Required Qualifications A Ph.D. in Neuroscience, Molecular Biology, or Microbiology  in Public Health, Clinical Psychology, Health Psychology, or a related discipline Ph.D./Ed.D. (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date) Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Good communication and interpersonal skills are preferred to facilitate interactions with faculty and students. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 2cbbb925 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Research Faculty/Instructor Research Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Center for Health Sciences OSU-Center for Health Sciences Minimum Education Level PhD