    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/instructor-electrical-electronics-instrumentation-230125-okmulgee-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Instructor – Electrical/Electronics Instrumentation #230125",
      "description": "Instructor – Electrical/Electronics Instrumentation #230125 - Okmulgee, Oklahoma, United States OKState.edu Applicant Login My Settings University Human Resources MENU Open Main Menu CLOSE Close Main Menu Home All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Home All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Applicant Login My Settings Kiosk mode Instructor – Electrical/Electronics Instrumentation #230125 Apply Now Instructor – Electrical/Electronics Instrumentation #230125 494888 Okmulgee INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY (OKM) Faculty Bachelor's degree Add to favorites View favorites Campus OSU-Institute of Technology Contact Name & Email Paula Harrold, paula.harrold@okstate.edu Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 7:30am-4:30pm with occasional evenings and weekends. May require availability for evening courses. Appointment Length Regular Continuous/Until Further Notice Hiring Range $50,000 - $55,000 Salary Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, please include a resume, cover letter and contact information for three professional references. About this Position GENERAL SUMMARY: This teaching position includes designing and facilitating learning environments in applied science degree programs. The programs award an Associate in Applied Science degree in Engineering Technologies with a specialization in Electrical Electronics and Bachelor of Technology degree in Instrumentation Technology. The focus of this instructional position will be in the operation, design, installation, repair and maintenance of systems typically found in manufacturing, processing, and utility industries. The main focus of this instructional position will be in the areas on automated measurement and control of pressure, temperature, flow, and level. Required Qualifications Education : Bachelor’s degree in Electrical, Electronics, Mechanical Engineering or related discipline from an accredited college or university; master’s degree strongly preferred. Other combinations of education and industry experience may be substituted for degree requirement with appropriate approval. Experience: Evidences a history of demonstrating ethical and professional behavior. Five (5) years documented successful work experience in related industry. Teaching experience in Higher Education preferred. Demonstrated success in collaborating with various constituencies. Certifications, Registrations, and/or Licenses: Licensure/Certification: Valid Oklahoma driver’s license. Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Skills and Abilities : Ability to plan, organize and fulfill complex initiatives. Computer skills to include electronic communications, word processing, and the ability to use specific software associated with the position are necessary. Ability to maintain high standards of work, initiative, commitment, ethics, professional responsibility and judgment. Ability to work effectively with and promote various populations. Superior interpersonal skills—including the ability to effectively recognize and resolve complex problems in a constructive manner. Must exhibit characteristics of a team player, willing to take initiative and assume responsibility. Ability to foster and support innovation and excellence. Communication Skills : Must demonstrate excellent oral and written communication skills. Must possess excellent interpersonal skills, with the ability to effectively recognize and resolve conflict. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert ba4fe549 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic Services/Student Support Faculty/Instructor Academic Services/Student Support Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Okmulgee, Oklahoma, United States Okmulgee, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Institute of Technology OSU-Institute of Technology Minimum Education Level Bachelor's degree Bachelor's degree First Name (required) 88056c24 Last Name (required) 493bb17f Email (required) d1a279ef Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) a140fd10 Last Name (required) c75e382a Email (required) add0df6d Save this job for later 563f36b6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Postdoctoral Fellow in Biology AF9026 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Adjunct Faculty - Construction #DD9902 Okmulgee INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY (OKM) Assistant Dean - School of Technology, Arts, Sciences, & Health #DS9962 Okmulgee INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY (OKM) Apply Now! First Name (required) 803e1eae Last Name (required) dfc6b595 Email (required) 848dba36 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you University Human Resources Part of the System Operations Oklahoma State University 201 General Academic Building Oklahoma State University Stillwater, OK 74078 (map) (405) 744-5449 | Contact Us Follow US News Events Social Media Directory Facebook LinkedIn Oklahoma State University Campus & Parking Maps All OSU Institutions Careers @ OSU Hire OSU Grads © 2026 Oklahoma State University. All rights reserved. Accessibility Services Campus Safety Access & Community Impact EEO Statement Ethics Point Privacy Notice Terms of Service Trademarks Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies, which may impact your user exper