    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-engineering-technologies-dd9950-tulsa-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "UniversityHuman Resources",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Engineering Technologies #DD9950 - Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States OKState.edu Applicant Login My Settings University Human Resources MENU Open Main Menu CLOSE Close Main Menu Home All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Home All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Applicant Login My Settings Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Engineering Technologies #DD9950 Apply Now Adjunct Faculty - Engineering Technologies #DD9950 494864 Tulsa INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY (OKM) Adjunct/Temp Faculty Associate's degree Add to favorites View favorites Campus OSU-Institute of Technology Contact Name & Email Paula Harrold, paula.harrold@okstate.edu Work Schedule Variable schedule. Monday, Tuesday, and Thursday night classes in Tulsa, OK. Weekends as needed. Appointment Length 12 months or less Hiring Range $ - $ Commensurate with education and experience Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by to ensure full consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, please include a resume, cover letter and contact information for three professional references. About this Position GENERAL SUMMARY: This position will facilitate learning for the Engineering Technologies program for evening courses located in Tulsa, OK.  Courses are based on AC/DC circuits, Digital Systems, introduction to PLCs, and Electronic Control Devices. Required Qualifications Education : Associate’s degree in Engineering Technologies or a related field from an accredited university or college, or certification from an industry recognized technical training program. Bachelor degree preferred. Other combinations of education and industry experience may be substituted for degree/certification requirements. Experience: Evidences a history of demonstrating ethical and professional behavior. 3+ years of evidenced Engineering Technologies experience. Hands-on PLC troubleshooting and programming experience. Teaching experience preferred. Demonstrated success in collaborating with various constituencies. Certifications, Registrations, and/or Licenses: Licensure/Certification: Valid Oklahoma driver’s license. Electrical Journeyman license. Preference given to an individual that is authorized to teach OSHA-30 general industry. Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Skills and Abilities : Ability to plan, organize and fulfill complex initiatives. Computer skills to include electronic communications, word processing, and the ability to use specific software associated with the position are necessary. Ability to maintain high standards of work, initiative, commitment, ethics, professional responsibility and judgment. Ability to work effectively with and promote various populations. Superior interpersonal skills—including the ability to effectively recognize and resolve complex problems in a constructive manner. Must exhibit characteristics of a team player, willing to take initiative and assume responsibility. Ability to foster and support innovation and excellence. Communication Skills : Must demonstrate excellent oral and written communication skills. Must possess excellent interpersonal skills, with the ability to effectively recognize and resolve conflict. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 770e6c72 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Adjunct/Temp Faculty Adjunct/Temp Faculty Locations Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Institute of Technology OSU-Institute of Technology Minimum Education Level Associate's degree Associate's degree First Name (required) fdd18173 Last Name (required) 649c2336 Email (required) 93276c54 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) fbf20a66 Last Name (required) 563469a2 Email (required) 52034845 Save this job for later 614d015a Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or click